{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe completion-verification close gate chronically fails in ways that leave no verdict: runaway duplicate tool-call loops (one live run repeated an identical search_files call 144x), request-budget exhaustion that dies verdict-less (the --force-close trap: a resource exhaustion is not a verdict, and the gate's only documented exit is --force-close), a recovery path that fans out one isolated evidence run per criterion (operator-ruled unapproved: c9f7's shape is 22 criteria x 20-request budget = 440 requests worst case with ~2.67M context chars re-sent), and a flat 100,000-char recovery context bound (completion_recovery.py:68) that refuses the live 121,147-char ticket c9f7 forever because ticket context is append-only and can only grow. Each failure was patched separately across four exhausted close attempts on epic e369; this epic reworks the verifier's context management as one design so exhaustion is bounded, verified progress survives failures, and every run with progress ends in a scored, signed verdict.\n\n## Approach\n\nRework along seams that already exist, generalizing only where multiple LLM workflows already share code (the agent_call.py tool-wrapping seam armed for every tool-bearing run, and model_classes.py model knowledge); everything specific to completion semantics — the verdict bank, criterion identity, context assembly, verdict coverage — stays completion-local in the workflow modules. Child responsibilities, each delivered by one child:\n\n- **Context ceilings** — replace the flat recovery char bound with a physical ceiling derived from the resolved verifier model's own context window plus an economic ceiling bounding total re-send spend, preserving the d59e invariants (no elision, zero billable calls on refusal).\n- **Duplicate-call damping** — memoize duplicate read-only tool calls at the shared agent-call seam and steer the model off repeats with static nudges; the shipped distinct-ratio runaway actuator stays as the abort backstop.\n- **Banked, batched verification** — record per-criterion verdicts incrementally to a run-scoped bank; replace the per-criterion recovery fan-out with batched successor runs over the unverified remainder under a request-denominated budget pool; finalize to a full-coverage verdict whenever any progress is banked, with a deterministic no-LLM fallback so a run with banked progress can never die verdict-less.\n- **Context pre-loading** — pre-fetch ranked file_impact contents into the fenced verifier context under a budget clamp with a per-file full/skeleton manifest, cutting agentic read round-trips (live traces show 67-82% of distinct file reads are covered by subtree file_impact).\n- **Interim evidence-run insurance** — single-criterion evidence-run survival hardening that ships only while the fan-out it patches still exists.\n\nSequencing is encoded as dependency edges: ceilings first (smallest change; unblocks re-certifications refused at preflight today), then duplicate-call damping (immediate waste cut for every agentic workflow), then the banked/batched core rework, then pre-loading (its improvement is only measurable against the post-rework baseline).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A completion verification whose primary run dies in a typed failure (budget exhaustion, runaway loop, or token exhaustion) with at least one criterion verdict banked ends in a full-coverage verdict instead of a verdict-less error — delivered by the banked-verification child; checked by its unit suite and a live Bedrock run recorded on that child.\n- [ ] No completion code path launches one isolated LLM run per criterion — delivered by the banked-verification child; checked by grep over src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py showing the fan-out removed, plus its unit suite.\n- [ ] The recovery preflight accepts the live c9f7 shape (121,147 chars x 22 criteria) under the two-ceiling bound with the d59e invariants intact — delivered by the context-ceilings child; checked by its held-out unit oracle and a live run recorded on that child.\n- [ ] Duplicate read-only tool calls inside one agentic run are served from a memo with a static nudge instead of re-executing, with the runaway actuator's window math unchanged — delivered by the duplicate-call damping child; checked by its unit tests and a live Bedrock capture recorded on that child.\n- [ ] The completion verifier's context pre-loads ranked file_impact contents with a full/skeleton manifest and reduces live request counts by at least 20% with verdict class unchanged versus the post-rework baseline — delivered by the pre-loading child; checked per that child's live A/B acceptance criteria."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786047326985832001,"uuid":"ea806697-6429-4865-ba16-9a6b1f27288d"}